[SPEAKER_02]: It's the same, but people might be doing it for completely different, let's say, reasons or intentions.

165
00:19:22,966 --> 00:19:24,567
[SPEAKER_02]: And so, that would be the factor.

166
00:19:25,688 --> 00:19:27,889
[SPEAKER_02]: An intention, by the way, is not publicly observable.

167
00:19:28,370 --> 00:19:31,112
[SPEAKER_02]: One's behavior is what is publicly observable.

168
00:19:31,132 --> 00:19:32,733
[SPEAKER_02]: That's what a scientist can study.

169
00:19:33,113 --> 00:19:34,955
[SPEAKER_02]: Put a camera there, look at it from the outside.

170
00:19:35,415 --> 00:19:38,598
[SPEAKER_02]: But why someone is doing what they're doing,

171
00:19:39,418 --> 00:19:41,620
[SPEAKER_02]: That can, at best, be inferred.

172
00:19:42,180 --> 00:19:46,284
[SPEAKER_02]: And it is impossible to abandon doubt from the outside.

173
00:19:46,784 --> 00:20:02,156
[SPEAKER_02]: That can only be done when one takes up this first-person, present-tense perspective, that's a sort of privileged point of view, where you see yourself doing what you are doing, while you are doing it, including your reasons for doing it.

174
00:20:02,276 --> 00:20:07,340
[SPEAKER_00]: So, basically, if you might be choosing to

