00:38:29,286 --> 00:38:33,308
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, the next level, let's say, you could say the person takes on celibacy.

349
00:38:34,008 --> 00:38:35,769
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, that will require a little bit more

350
00:38:36,450 --> 00:38:43,051
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, quite a bit more recognition of the intention behind directions to to be able to practically do it.

351
00:38:45,394 --> 00:38:53,478
[SPEAKER_00]: Refrain from sexual activity, but your mind is going to have those intentions there, because it's used to go in that direction.

352
00:38:53,978 --> 00:39:01,482
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, if you don't recognize them, you will find yourself, sooner or later, about to engage in sexual activity.

353
00:39:01,922 --> 00:39:05,103
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it will force you to recognize the intention behind your actions as well.

354
00:39:06,044 --> 00:39:10,986
[SPEAKER_00]: And, it's just that same... it's that progression.

355
00:39:11,046 --> 00:39:11,366
[SPEAKER_00]: So,

356
00:39:13,647 --> 00:39:22,251
[SPEAKER_00]: From the beginning all the way to the end, it's just a refinement of a person being able to see the intentions behind their actions more clearly.

357
00:39:22,771 --> 00:39:27,693
[SPEAKER_00]: In fact, with the hindrances, when it comes to abandoning the hindrances, usually it's taken as

358
00:39:28,773 --> 00:39:36,220
[SPEAKER_00]: It's about focusing on objects and not experiencing other objects anymore.

359
00:39:36,440 --> 00:39:52,635
[SPEAKER_00]: But, when the suttas explain what samādhi is, it's always about purifying the mind from unwholesome things, in the same way that you are purifying your behavior from unwholesome things, from unwholesome intentions.

360
00:39:52,795 --> 00:39:54,796
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why, in fact,

361
00:39:55,908 --> 00:40:11,572
[SPEAKER_00]: There is no way for a person who... for a person to get samādhi that is in accordance with the Middle Way, if they haven't developed their body and speech in accordance with the Middle Way beforehand.

362
00:40:12,092 --> 00:40:22,454
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it's actually a much subtler version of... a more subtle instance of the same principle, of purifying unwholesome intentions.

363
00:40:23,174 --> 00:40:25,395
[SPEAKER_00]: So the saying would then...

364
00:40:26,896 --> 00:40:28,276
[SPEAKER_00]: The same thing that you did.

365
00:40:29,137 --> 00:40:33,539
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, I recognize this intention to do this or that with my body.

366
00:40:33,999 --> 00:40:35,320
[SPEAKER_00]: I choose not to engage with it.

367
00:40:36,001 --> 00:40:38,402
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you will start to see the same thing with your mind.

368
00:40:38,922 --> 00:40:41,083
[SPEAKER_00]: I see a hindrance of sensuality.

369
00:40:41,584 --> 00:40:42,924
[SPEAKER_00]: I see a hindrance of ill-will.

370
00:40:43,725 --> 00:40:48,147
[SPEAKER_00]: And, obviously, the saying no to it is much coarser.

371
00:40:48,267 --> 00:40:51,469
[SPEAKER_00]: It's much... it's done, you know, on a much more subtler level.

372
00:40:51,929 --> 00:40:57,230
[SPEAKER_00]: But it would be the same as you choosing not to kill when there is an intention to kill, for example.

373
00:40:57,910 --> 00:41:03,711
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even that is also just about intention behind your actions.

374
00:41:03,731 --> 00:41:08,092
[SPEAKER_00]: There is nothing, nothing in the dhamma that is about something else.

375
00:41:08,772 --> 00:41:14,853
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, okay, I watch my intention behind the actions and then now, when it comes to samādhi, now it's time to do something different.

376
00:41:15,393 --> 00:41:18,054
[SPEAKER_00]: So, because that's usually the perception.

377
00:41:18,354 --> 00:41:18,714
[SPEAKER_00]: And then,

378
00:41:20,235 --> 00:41:23,358
[SPEAKER_00]: There is no connection then between your sīla and your samādhi.

379
00:41:23,398 --> 00:41:26,241
[SPEAKER_00]: It's kind of like just two different things.

380
00:41:26,802 --> 00:41:32,888
[SPEAKER_00]: So... And then, yeah, once you start seeing your intentions behind your actions,

381
00:41:34,560 --> 00:41:46,425
[SPEAKER_00]: You recognize... you are able, once you see them to a certain extent, let's say, which is a sign of the mind, the prerequisite for the right view, then you can see, oh, these intentions are suffering.

382
00:41:46,805 --> 00:41:48,466
[SPEAKER_00]: These intentions are the origin of suffering.

383
00:41:49,327 --> 00:41:53,768
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if I... the cessation of these intentions is the cessation of suffering.

384
00:41:54,969 --> 00:42:03,613
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you will get to understand the Four Noble Truths once you are, to a very, very high degree, able to see the intention behind your actions.

385
00:42:04,763 --> 00:42:20,036
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, that's like you are fully established in that principle of the Middle Way to the point where now you can't forget it anymore.

386
00:42:20,276 --> 00:42:20,516
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

